# SRG-APP-000391-AU-002290  -  CAT II
# The Central Log Server must be configured to accept the DoW common access
# card (CAC) credential to support identity management and personal
# authentication.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations, then kept
# by hand. Edit this file to change how this requirement is assessed here;
# it is read at run time. Regenerating refreshes the benchmark text in place
# and leaves the criteria, the determination and any verification block as
# they are.

id:              SRG-APP-000391-AU-002290
group:           V-206506
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      documented
cci:             CCI-001953
control_rev5:    IA-2

contribution:    Splunk Enterprise 10.4.2 can accept a CAC/PIV certificate as the login
                 credential on its own: web.conf [settings] enableCertBasedUserAuth turns
                 on certificate-based user authentication, requireClientCert makes Splunk
                 Web demand the client certificate, and certBasedUserAuthMethod selects how
                 the user identity is taken from the card certificate (CommonName, EDIPI,
                 or PIV).

governs:         web.conf - Configures the Splunk Web interface.

check:           web.conf [settings] enableCertBasedUserAuth in true|True|TRUE|t|1|yes
check:           web.conf [settings] requireClientCert in true|True|TRUE|t|1|yes
check:           web.conf [settings] certBasedUserAuthMethod in CommonName|EDIPI|PIV
# --- vendor verification: generated, do not edit by hand
vendor:          web.conf [settings] certBasedUserAuthMethod https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/manage-users-and-security/10.4/authenticate-into-splunk-enterprise-using-hardware/configure-splunk-enterprise-to-use-a-common-access-card-for-authentication
vendor:          web.conf [settings] enableCertBasedUserAuth https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/manage-users-and-security/10.4/authenticate-into-splunk-enterprise-using-hardware/configure-splunk-enterprise-to-use-a-common-access-card-for-authentication
vendor:          web.conf [settings] requireClientCert https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/manage-users-and-security/10.4/authenticate-into-splunk-enterprise-using-hardware/configure-splunk-enterprise-to-use-a-common-access-card-for-authentication
# --- end vendor verification

external:        Card reader and PKI middleware at the workstation - carried by the client
                 operating system.
external:        DoD PKI trust anchor and issuing CA chain - carried by the organization's
                 PKI; supplied to the product through web.conf sslRootCAPath or its
                 documented fallback to the server.conf setting of the same name, which is
                 why no condition is written over the web.conf value alone.
external:        Where the approved implementation terminates PKI upstream instead,
                 SPLK-CL-000490's own fix names an Apache, IIS, F5, or SAML SSO proxy;
                 credential acceptance is then carried by that proxy and the native
                 web.conf settings may legitimately be absent.
external:        Applicability: SPLK-CL-000490 records this check as Not Applicable on a
                 distributed-deployment instance running with the web interface disabled.

citation:        splunk-spec-files/web.conf.spec:16 ([settings]), :120
                 (enableCertBasedUserAuth, default false), :133 (certBasedUserAuthMethod,
                 values CommonName|EDIPI|PIV, no default), :151 (requireClientCert, default
                 false); SPLK-CL-000490 check and fix text
finding:         Splunk Web is not configured to accept a CAC/PIV certificate as a login
                 credential - certificate-based user authentication is not enabled in
                 web.conf [settings] (enableCertBasedUserAuth, requireClientCert,
                 certBasedUserAuthMethod) and no approved PKI-terminating SSO proxy was
                 presented as the implementation; this determination is from the
                 perspective of the application layer alone.
